SUMMARY:AMC150 Worcester Chapter TrailsFest: 20s & 30s East-West Trail Hik
 e - Prospect Hill and Newton Hill
LOCATION:126 Salisbury St #10\nWorcester\, MA
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 6\, 2026 | 8:30 AM\nhttps://activities.outdoor
 s.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX0000016iFV2AY/\nJoin the Worcester Chapter 20s & 
 30s on a ~4 mile hike along a segment of the East-West Trail\, which trave
 rses the city of Worcester over 14 miles. This hike will take us through 
 Institute Park\, Salisbury Park\, and Elm Park over a variety of terrain -
 - from the trails up to Newton Hill to walking through neighborhoods near 
 Prospect Hill. One notable landmark on the hike is Bancroft Tower\, a 125-
 year-old 56-foot-high (17 m) tower of granite and natural stone. We will p
 lan on ending our hike at Bancroft Tower and spending some time there. Des
 pite the short mileage\, there is an expected elevation gain of around 630
  ft throughout the hike centered around Prospect Hill and Newton Hill.Part
 icipants must bring:Minimum 1 liter of waterSnacks as necessaryLayers as t
 he weather dictates\, including outer shellHiking shoes or boots with good
  treadBackpack to carry gearConfirmed participants can expect an email a f
 ew days before the activity with weather\, meeting location\, and parking 
 details.After this trip\, please join us for the AMC150 Worcester Chapter 
 TrailsFest 2026\, taking place Saturday\, June 6\, 2026 at Institute Park 
 in Worcester! TrailsFest\, which has been held annually since 2018\, coinc
 ides with National Trails Day and is co-hosted by a group of organizations
  including the Appalachian Mountain Club and Park Spirit.At this event\, w
 e celebrate trails in all their forms\, including hiking trails\, bike pat
 hs\, waterways\, and climbing routes. Here is what the day will look like:
 Morning through 12pm: Activities like this one throughout the area.12pm to
  4:00pm: AMC150 Worcester Chapter TrailsFest celebration at Institute Park
 . Food\, live music\, speakers\, friends\, and fun!BYO non-alcoholic bever
 ages and a chair.Bring yourself\, your friends and family\, and spread the
  word!In 2026\, the Appalachian Mountain Club is celebrating 150 years of 
 protecting\, enjoying\, and understanding the outdoors! At the heart of th
 e celebration is the AMC 150th Outdoor Relay—a connected series of outdo
 or adventures traveling from Virginia to Maine with a commemorative AMC fl
 ag carried along the entire route.
END:VEVENT
